  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Epirot and Macedonian folk instrumental tradition formed after the Albanian-Greek Ottoman clarinet trade of the 1830s-1870s and codified on disc by Kitsos Harisiadis, Vasilis Soukas and Petroloukas Chalkias, in which a B-flat or C klarino plays free-rhythm miroloi laments and then aksak dance suites (tsamiko 3/4, syrtos 2/4, beratis 8/8) at 60-130 BPM over a laouto strum-drone with heterophonic violi, using chalumeau-register smears, microtonal bends and long circular-breathed phrases.",
